<title>NETHERLANDS: HIM finalises Furness purchase.</title>
<headline>HIM finalises Furness purchase.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch industrial investment firm Hollandia Industriele Maatschappij (HIM) said on Monday it had legally gained ownership of the Furness shares from Pakhoed.</p>
<p>With the purchase, HIM said it expected a 1996 profit of about three million guilders.</p>
<p>The company also expects to pay an interim dividend of 4.15 guilders per share on December 30, in cash or in stock from the tax-free share premium reserve. Under the latter payment, one new share can be obtained for every 17 shares held.</p>
<p>After payment of this interim dividend, the intrinsic value of the shares will amount to 70 guilders, HIM said in a statement.</p>
<p>HIM and Pakhoed reached agreement in August on the sale of Pakhoed's Furness unit which combines port activities, car dealerships and logistics division.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
